            "fixedCode": "fn main() {\n    let value = 7;\n    let p = &value as *const i32;\n    println!(\"{}\", unsafe { *p });\n}",
            "explanation": "Dereferencing a raw pointer is an unsafe operation, so the compiler requires it inside an unsafe block where the programmer takes responsibility for its safety."
